diff --git a/ANSWER.md b/ANSWER.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4444586
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ANSWER.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Why nightly-review was silent
+
+The job did run (launchctl print: `runs = 6`, `last exit code = 1`). It failed, and the failure reporter died too. The cause is two stacked bugs, visible in `Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`.
+
+1. **`claude` fails with "Not logged in".** launchd gives the job no `USER` (or `HOME`) in its environment, so the CLI can't find its login in the keychain. The review exits non-zero every night.
+2. **`status=$?` in `bin/nightly-review.zsh` is fatal in zsh.** `status` is a read-only builtin, so the script dies with `read-only variable: status`. That happens before the `notify.sh` failure call, so no failure note is ever sent.
+
+Together these meant no summary and no failure message.
+
+## Fixes
+- Script: `status` → `rc`. Also added `< /dev/null` to the `claude -p` call so it can't wait on stdin.
+- Plist: added `USER=vk` and `HOME=/Users/vk` under `EnvironmentVariables`.
+
+## To apply and verify
+The plist is loaded in launchd, so reload it:
+`launchctl bootout gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review; launchctl bootstrap gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist; launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`
+
+Then check that you get the Telegram message and that the run takes a plausible time. I couldn't run any of this here.
+
+## Not verified
+- `claude` has to be on the plist PATH (`/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:...`). If it lives in `~/.local/bin`, add that to PATH.
+- `notify.sh` reads its token from the keychain, which should work in the gui domain.
+- Changes are in this snapshot only. Copy them to your real home dir.
